.nh
.TH go-md2man 1 "January 2015" go-md2man "User Manual"

.SH "نام (NAME)"
go-md2man \- Convert markdown files into manpages


.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
\fBgo-md2man\fP [\fB-in\fP=\fI/path/to/md/file\fP] [\fB-out\fP=\fI/path/to/output\fP]


.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
\fBgo-md2man\fP converts standard markdown formatted documents into manpages. It is
written purely in Go so as to reduce dependencies on 3rd party libs.

.PP
By default, the input is stdin and the output is stdout.


.SH "گزینه‌ها (OPTIONS)"
.TP
\fB-in=\fP\fIfile\fP
Path to markdown file to be processed.

Defaults to stdin.

.TP
\fB-out=\fP\fIfile\fP
Path to output processed file.

Defaults to stdout.


.SH "مثال‌ها (EXAMPLES)"
Convert the markdown file \fIgo-md2man.1.md\fP into a manpage:

.EX
go-md2man < go-md2man.1.md > go-md2man.1
.EE

.PP
Same, but using command line arguments instead of shell redirection:

.EX
go-md2man -in=go-md2man.1.md -out=go-md2man.1
.EE


.SH "تاریخچه (HISTORY)"
January 2015, Originally compiled by Brian Goff (cpuguy83@gmail.com).
